9286,-0.01397109,0.01297522,-0.00343364,0.05893465,-0.09411652,0.02434563,0.05294905,0.19343181,-0.03469747,-0.00041449,0.0279106,-0.08979223,-0.04965422,0.00676956,-0.01332143,0.0168556,0.02112931,0.11044993,-0.03450331,0.08947659,0.04382245,-0.05190129,-0.05623335,0.0083706,-0.05662904,0.04068726,0.03544336,-0.05890707,-0.01359673,0.10537203,-0.01477782,-0.0060146,-0.07444828,0.02496378,-0.01784441,0.01443545,-0.03361992,-0.05263914,-0.02041131,0.05825152,-0.00843712,-0.0257382,0.0014569,-0.05005313,-0.04451206,0.00387405,0.00978446,0.01955317,0.07554426,-0.02960066],"last_embed":{"hash":"1lk1xqb","tokens":399}}},"last_read":{"hash":"1lk1xqb","at":1778067900860},"class_name":"SmartSource","last_import":{"mtime":1774939523000,"size":5032,"at":1778067900861,"hash":"1lk1xqb"},"blocks":{"#---frontmatter---":[1,18],"#Artificial intelligence as an analytic approximation to evaluate associations between parental feeding behaviours and excess weight in Colombian preschoolers":[20,42],"#Artificial intelligence as an analytic approximation to evaluate associations between parental feeding behaviours and excess weight in Colombian preschoolers#{1}":[21,25],"#Artificial intelligence as an analytic approximation to evaluate associations between parental feeding behaviours and excess weight in Colombian preschoolers#📝 Benim Notlarım":[26,28],"#Artificial intelligence as an analytic approximation to evaluate associations between parental feeding behaviours and excess weight in Colombian preschoolers#📝 Benim Notlarım#{1}":[27,28],"#Artificial intelligence as an analytic approximation to evaluate associations between parental feeding behaviours and excess weight in Colombian preschoolers#🟡 Genel Bilgiler (Sarı)":[29,31],"#Artificial intelligence as an analytic approximation to evaluate associations between parental feeding behaviours and excess weight in Colombian preschoolers#🟢 Yöntem & Örneklem (Yeşil)":[32,34],"#Artificial intelligence as an analytic approximation to evaluate associations between parental feeding behaviours and excess weight in Colombian preschoolers#🟢 Yöntem & Örneklem (Yeşil)#{1}":[33,34],"#Artificial intelligence as an analytic approximation to evaluate associations between parental feeding behaviours and excess weight in Colombian preschoolers#🔴 Bulgular (Kırmızı)":[35,37],"#Artificial intelligence as an analytic approximation to evaluate associations between parental feeding behaviours and excess weight in Colombian preschoolers#🔴 Bulgular (Kırmızı)#{1}":[36,37],"#Artificial intelligence as an analytic approximation to evaluate associations between parental feeding behaviours and excess weight in Colombian preschoolers#🔵 Sonuç / Conclusions (Mavi)":[38,40],"#Artificial intelligence as an analytic approximation to evaluate associations between parental feeding behaviours and excess weight in Colombian preschoolers#🔵 Sonuç / Conclusions (Mavi)#{1}":[39,40],"#Artificial intelligence as an analytic approximation to evaluate associations between parental feeding behaviours and excess weight in Colombian preschoolers#🟠 Limitasyonlar (Turuncu)":[41,42]},"outlinks":[{"title":"Görüntüle","target":"zotero://select/library/items/DKEWMX8X","line":22},{"title":"Sayfa 1","target":"zotero://open-pdf/library/items/KG4YU6RY?page=1&annotation=6RHJP2CE","line":33},{"title":"Sayfa 3","target":"zotero://open-pdf/library/items/KG4YU6RY?page=3&annotation=7V6Q3I6A","line":33},{"title":"Sayfa 4","target":"zotero://open-pdf/library/items/KG4YU6RY?page=4&annotation=HQ4T4552","line":36},{"title":"Sayfa 5","target":"zotero://open-pdf/library/items/KG4YU6RY?page=5&annotation=JSDMG5I9","line":36},{"title":"Sayfa 6","target":"zotero://open-pdf/library/items/KG4YU6RY?page=6&annotation=Z23ZDZGZ","line":39}],"metadata":{"Title":"Artificial intelligence as an analytic approximation to evaluate associations between parental feeding behaviours and excess weight in Colombian preschoolers","Authors":"Edna M. Gamboa, Claudia I. Amaya, Antonio Bahamonde","Year":2021,"DOI":"10.1017/S0007114520003797","Nitelik":null,"Alan":null,"Konu":null,"AI_Methodology":null,"Layer_Focus":null,"Model_Asamasi":null,"Proposed_Tool":null,"Methods":". Therefore, the aim of this study was to evaluate the relationship between parents’ practices related to feeding their children and excess weight in preschoolers in Bucaramanga, Colombia, using artificial intelligence.Two alternative methods were used to determine the parental practices that most affected OW in the children. First, the results obtained with Artificial Intelligence techniques are presented, namely, techniques for selecting subsets of variables (feature subset selection) with machine learning tasks. This technique used programmes implemented in Python with scikit-learn library.","Findings":"Table 2 presents the results from the selection of variables using Recursive Feature Elimination, the artificial intelligence method described previously. This was based on two sets of variables and used the selection method. The first group includes the variables from all three groups, represented by G1 þ G2 þ G3. The selection that was obtained is limited to three variables: 31_2, 31_5 and 67. An AUC of 0·676 was obtained only with these variables. Note that the variables 31_2 and 31_5 correspond to the group of questions inquiring about whether food or drinks were used to control the children’s behaviour.Actually, the results from the artificial intelligence approach described in this paper agreed with findings obtained by traditional methods and also showed additional evidences.","Conclusions":"Another strength that is worth noting is the methodological approach that was applied using artificial intelligence techniques to evaluate the association of interest to this study. This application, which is new in the field of nutrition, improves the robustness of the evidence that is generated, thereby contributing to the internal validity of the findings","Limitations":"","User_Notes":"figür 2 kiş bes açıklamak için çok iyi."},"task_lines":[],"tasks":{},"codeblock_ranges":[],"last_embed":{"hash":"1lk1xqb","at":1774939758329},"key":"Augmented Dietitian/gamboaArtificialIntelligenceAnalytic2021a.md"},
